      "finding": "The new len==0 branch passes JSContext* ctx to js_empty_string(JSRuntime* rt). The helper reads rt->atom_array; these are different native owner types. This is a concrete call-signature mismatch and an unsafe owner interpretation if admitted despite its diagnostic.",
      "proposed_exact_old": "return js_empty_string(ctx);",
      "proposed_exact_new": "return js_empty_string(ctx->rt);",
      "native_failure_observed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "byte_pointer_type",
      "severity": "c_constraint_diagnostic",
      "evidence": [
        "actual_byte_helper",
        "new_latin1_body"
      ],
      "finding": "The new const uint8_t* (unsigned char*) argument is passed to const char*. Plain char remains a distinct C type under -funsigned-char. Use an explicit character-storage reinterpretation for the original byte-copy helper.",
      "proposed_exact_old": "return js_new_string8_len(ctx, buf, (int)len);",
      "proposed_exact_new": "return js_new_string8_len(ctx, (const char *)buf, (int)len);",
      "native_failure_observed": false
    }
  ],
